    {
      "id": "NONFINDING-CHARACTER-LOD-TABLE-INDEX-001",
      "disposition": "The inspected public CharacterLod owner cannot reach its three-element vertex table with an out-of-range u8 through its normal TryFrom admission.",
      "trace": "CharacterLod has a private u8 field and TryFrom admits only the re-exported MHR MIN_LOD through MAX_LOD inclusive. At 95e those constants are 4 and 6, so the admitted index self.0 - MIN_CHARACTER_LOD is 0, 1 or 2, exactly within the three-element [2461, 971, 595] table. The creator CLI declares the same range, load_body_model calls TryFrom before Mhr::from_files, and the GLB export validator calls TryFrom. This is source and bounded integer reasoning; no constructor, input, widget, export or test was executed.",
      "remaining": "This does not prove model asset vertex counts, topology, UI widget output, every native MHR caller or full exporter admission. The model control declares a slider range but its expect and actual widget behavior were not executed. Other lenses, producers, historical aliases and 059 native-geometry contract remain open."
    }
